; Coverage configuration for the bundled consumer example (P9-15, G9-12).
;
; The example is a consumer service with its own settings and package root, so
; it is not measured by the issuer's --cov=auth_user_service gate. Before this
; file the example's CI job ran with no --cov-fail-under at all, which meant the
; example's coverage could regress silently while the issuer's held at 100%.
;
; The number this gate enforces is not 100 and is not meant to be: the point is
; that it is declared, justified, and enforced. Every omission below is named
; and reasoned, exactly as .coveragerc names the issuer's.
;
; Measured at 95.68% (branch) when the gate was introduced; pytest.ini declares
; the floor at 95. What sits in the remaining gap, so it is visible rather than
; absorbed:
;   * app/routes/category.py — three generic `except Exception ->
;     handle_route_exception` fallbacks. Not authorization branches; the
;     unique-name collision that used to land in one of them now answers 409 on
;     its own branch, and the three not-found branches are covered.
;   * controllers/dashboard.py — the hour/day/year time-range variants and the
;     invalid-range guard of the reporting window helper.
;   * app/routes/dashboard.py — one reporting route with no unit caller.
; None is an authorization or audit surface. Raising the floor is a one-line
; change once they are covered.

[run]
source = fastapi_full
branch = True
omit =
    ; ASGI entrypoint — process wiring, exercised by the example-smoke
    ; workflow's real stack rather than by unit tests. Mirrors the issuer's
    ; auth_user_service/main.py omission.
    */fastapi_full/main.py
    ; Settings bootstrap. Mirrors the issuer's core/config.py omission: the
    ; unit environment supplies its own settings through tests/conftest.py, so
    ; the real construction path is never the one under test.
    */fastapi_full/core/config.py
    ; The fa-auth SSE bridge consumer. A live-stack surface by construction —
    ; it holds an open event stream against a running issuer — so it has no
    ; unit coverage, the same reason the issuer omits its live-tested-only
    ; routes rather than pretending a mock proves them.
    */fastapi_full/core/events.py
    ; Built only when this deployment enables remote API-key introspection
    ; (API_KEY_INTROSPECTION_ENABLED=true). The unit environment never enables
    ; it, so the route bodies are unreachable here. The contract they
    ; demonstrate is proven where it belongs: the workspace conformance
    ; harness's API-key principal section (§3.12) and the issuer's own suites.
    */fastapi_full/app/routes/api_key_category.py
    ; Migration scripts. Applied and asserted against real engines by the
    ; Layer B suite, not by this unit gate. Mirrors the issuer's alembic omit.
    */fastapi_full/alembic/*
    ; The tests themselves.
    */fastapi_full/tests/*

[report]
show_missing = True
exclude_lines =
    pragma: no cover
    if __name__ == .__main__.:
    raise NotImplementedError
    @abstractmethod
    if TYPE_CHECKING:
